    "Off, the stage is the plant and the marks along the foot, in no language at all." : {
      "comment" : "Under that switch. Says what is left when the words go, rather than what is lost.",
      "localizations" : {
        "da" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Slået fra er der planten og mærkerne langs bunden, på slet intet sprog."
          }
        },
        "es" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Apagado, quedan la planta y las marcas del pie, en ningún idioma."
          }
        },
        "fr" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Désactivé, il reste la plante et les marques en bas, dans aucune langue."
          }
        },
        "it" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Spento, restano la pianta e i segni in basso, in nessuna lingua."
          }
        },
        "nb" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Slått av står planten og merkene langs bunnen igjen, på ikke noe språk."
          }
        },
        "nl" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Uit blijven de plant en de tekens onderaan over, in geen enkele taal."
          }
        },
        "sv" : {
          "stringUnit" : {
            "state" : "translated",
            "value" : "Avstängt återstår växten och märkena längs foten, på inget språk alls."
          }
        }
      }
    },
    "On a passing current" : {
      "comment" : "One of forty figurative places a seed is imagined passing through on its way to the ground. Offered, already filled in, as the answer to 'Where' on the note about a meeting, and anybody can type over it. The register is the seed's journey rather than real geography, so it wants the same unhurried, slightly literary voice in every language.",
